IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-groups`
IMPORT `sgc2-common`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 6 Division 2, sections 206 (auditors' remuneration), 207 (powers and duties of auditors as to reports on financial statements),
-- 208 (qualified privilege) and 208A (provisions indemnifying auditors). LAYER 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- Two readings run through this module. Where a duty carries no number of days ("immediately", or no time at all) the rule is written
-- and traced, and its time is an input (the s 52 input, or the section's own standard where the text gives one: notes/lest-without-deadline.md), and the decision function says "is in default" when
-- the act was not done (and, where the text says "immediately", not done immediately): the asker supplies those facts as at the time of asking.
-- Where the text makes a passive demand with no one named ("must be attached to or endorsed on", section 207(7)), only a decision function is written.

§ `The acts and parties of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `s 206 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 206(1)(c) prepare a statement showing particulars of all emoluments paid to the auditor or other person and of the services in respect of which the payments have been made`
    `s 206(1)(d) forward a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`
    `s 206(1)(e) lay the statement before the company in general meeting`
    `s 206(1A) undertake a review of the fees, expenses and emoluments of the auditor to determine whether the independence of the auditor has been compromised`
    `s 206(1A) send the outcome of the review to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`

DECLARE `s 207 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 207(1) report to the members`
    `s 207(1A) furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time`
    `s 207(9) report the matter in writing to the Registrar`
    `s 207(9A) report the matter to the Minister`

-- What an auditor asks to see under section 207(5), (6) and (10), and the one kind of register that subsection (11) takes out of those provisions.
DECLARE `s 207(5) access item` IS ONE OF
    `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register`
    `s 207(5) a register other than a register kept under Part 11A`
    `s 207(5) a register kept under Part 11A`

-- Whom the auditor asks for information and explanations under section 207(5), and under section 207(6).
DECLARE `s 207(5) person asked` IS ONE OF
    `s 207(5) an officer of the company`
    `s 207(5) an auditor of another company`
    `s 207(5) any other person`

DECLARE `s 207(6) person asked` IS ONE OF
    `s 207(6) an officer of a subsidiary corporation`
    `s 207(6) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation`
    `s 207(6) any other person`

-- Who a section 207(8) right belongs to.
DECLARE `s 207(8) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 207(8) an auditor of the company`
    `s 207(8) an agent authorised by the auditor in writing for the purpose`
    `s 207(8) any other person`

-- The persons and the conduct of section 207(10).
DECLARE `s 207(10) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 207(10) an officer of a company`
    `s 207(10) an officer of a subsidiary corporation`
    `s 207(10) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation`
    `s 207(10) any other person`

DECLARE `s 207(10) conduct` IS ONE OF
    `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)`
    `s 207(10)(b) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the parent company access in accordance with subsection (6)`
    `s 207(10)(c) refused or failed to give information or explanation as and when required under subsection (5) or (6)`
    `s 207(10)(d) otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed an auditor in the performance of the auditor's duties or the exercise of the auditor's powers under section 207`

§ `Section 206: auditors' remuneration`

-- (1): "If a company is served with a notice sent by or on behalf of -- (a) at least 5% of the total number of members of the company; or (b) the holders in aggregate of not less than 5% of the total number
-- of issued shares of the company (excluding treasury shares), requiring particulars of all emoluments ..." 5%: held times 20 is at least the total, and someone must hold something.
-- The notice must be one "requiring particulars of all emoluments paid to or receivable by the auditor ... in respect of services other than auditing services".
-- An "if" the text introduces: when it is not met the answer is JUST FALSE (marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1).
-- src:19728 | 206.—(1) If a company is served with a notice sent by or on behalf
-- src:19729 | of —
-- src:19731 | (a) at least 5% of the total number of members of the
-- src:19732 | company; or
-- src:19734 | (b) the holders in aggregate of not less than 5% of the total
-- src:19735 | number of issued shares of the company (excluding
-- src:19736 | treasury shares),
-- src:19741 | requiring particulars of all emoluments paid to or receivable by the
-- src:19742 | auditor of the company or any person who is a partner or employer or
-- src:19743 | employee of the auditor, by or from the company or any subsidiary
-- src:19744 | corporation in respect of services other than auditing services
-- src:19745 | rendered to the company, the company must immediately —
@ref s 206(1) (src:19728-19745)
GIVEN `the company has been served with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice requires particulars of all emoluments paid to or receivable by the auditor, or a partner or employer or employee of the auditor, in respect of services other than auditing services rendered to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members on whose behalf the notice was sent` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of issued shares held in aggregate by the holders on whose behalf the notice was sent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(1) the notice engages the duty of the company` MEANS
    IF     `the company has been served with the notice`
       AND `the notice requires particulars of all emoluments paid to or receivable by the auditor, or a partner or employer or employee of the auditor, in respect of services other than auditing services rendered to the company`
       AND (    (`the number of members on whose behalf the notice was sent` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of members on whose behalf the notice was sent` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `the total number of members of the company`)
             OR (`the number of issued shares held in aggregate by the holders on whose behalf the notice was sent` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of issued shares held in aggregate by the holders on whose behalf the notice was sent` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `the total number of issued shares of the company, excluding treasury shares`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company is served with a notice sent by or on behalf of -- (a) at least 5% of the total number of members of the company; or (b) the holders in aggregate of not less than 5% of the total number of issued shares of the company (excluding treasury shares), requiring particulars of all emoluments ..." (an "if" not met: marginal reading (a), fork line F-M1)

-- "the company must immediately -- (c) prepare ... a statement ..."
-- src:19747 | (c) prepare or cause to be prepared a statement showing
-- src:19748 | particulars of all emoluments paid to the auditor or other
-- src:19749 | person and of the services in respect of which the payments
-- src:19750 | have been made for the financial year immediately
-- src:19751 | preceding the service of such notice;
@ref s 206(1)(c) (src:19747-19751)
GIVEN `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has prepared or caused to be prepared the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(1)(c) the company is in default of the duty to prepare the statement` MEANS
    IF `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` AND (NOT (`the company has prepared or caused to be prepared the statement` AND `the company did so immediately`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must immediately -- (c) prepare or cause to be prepared a statement showing particulars of all emoluments paid to the auditor or other person" (a duty met, or not engaged: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

-- src:19753 | (d) forward a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to
-- src:19754 | receive notice of general meetings of the company; and
@ref s 206(1)(d) (src:19753-19754)
GIVEN `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has forwarded a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(1)(d) the company is in default of the duty to forward a copy of the statement` MEANS
    IF `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` AND (NOT (`the company has forwarded a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` AND `the company did so immediately`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must immediately -- (d) forward a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company" (a duty met, or not engaged: fork line F-D1)

-- src:19756 | (e) lay such statement before the company in general meeting.
@ref s 206(1)(e) (src:19756-19756)
GIVEN `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has laid the statement before the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(1)(e) the company is in default of the duty to lay the statement before the company in general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the notice engages the duty of the company under section 206(1)` AND (NOT (`the company has laid the statement before the company in general meeting` AND `the company did so immediately`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must immediately -- (e) lay such statement before the company in general meeting" (a duty met, or not engaged: fork line F-D1)

-- "immediately" has no number of days in the text: for each of the three rules below the section's own standard of time is the input `the period the standard of time allows, as found`, so a late act reaches BREACH (notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
@ref s 206(1)(c) (src:19756-19756)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("immediately") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 206 act`
`s 206(1)(c) the company must prepare the statement of the auditor's other emoluments` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 206(1)(c) prepare a statement showing particulars of all emoluments paid to the auditor or other person and of the services in respect of which the payments have been made`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "immediately" (s 206(1)(c)); the period is an input, as found (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not prepare the statement of the auditor's other emoluments that the notice required"

@ref s 206(1)(d) (src:19756-19756)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("immediately") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 206 act`
`s 206(1)(d) the company must forward a copy of the statement` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 206(1)(d) forward a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "immediately" (s 206(1)(d)); the period is an input, as found (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not forward a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings"

@ref s 206(1)(e) (src:19756-19756)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("immediately") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 206 act`
`s 206(1)(e) the company must lay the statement before the company in general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 206(1)(e) lay the statement before the company in general meeting`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "immediately" (s 206(1)(e)); the period is an input, as found (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lay the statement before the company in general meeting"

-- (1A): "Without affecting subsection (1), a public company must, under prescribed circumstances, undertake a review of the fees, expenses and emoluments of its auditor ...".
-- The circumstances are prescribed outside the text: asked as a fact. A company that is not a public company is outside the sentence (a scope limit with no "only": NOTHING, the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)).
-- src:19760 | (1A) Without affecting subsection (1), a public company must,
-- src:19761 | under prescribed circumstances, undertake a review of the fees,
-- src:19762 | expenses and emoluments of its auditor to determine whether the
-- src:19763 | independence of the auditor has been compromised, and the outcome
-- src:19764 | of the review must be sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of
-- src:19765 | general meetings of the company.
@ref s 206(1A) (src:19760-19765)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances are circumstances prescribed for such a review` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(1A) the duty of the public company to review the auditor's fees applies` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND `the circumstances are circumstances prescribed for such a review`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a public company must, under prescribed circumstances, undertake a review" -- what the prescribed circumstances are is left to regulations that are not among the sources (and a company that is not a public company is outside the sentence)

@ref s 206(1A) (src:19760-19765)
GIVEN `the duty of the public company to review the auditor's fees applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has undertaken the review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has sent the outcome of the review to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(1A) the company is in default of the duty to review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` MEANS
    IF `the duty of the public company to review the auditor's fees applies` AND (NOT (`the company has undertaken the review` AND `the company has sent the outcome of the review to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a public company must, under prescribed circumstances, undertake a review ... and the outcome of the review must be sent to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company" (a duty met, or not applying: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

-- No time is stated: the time allowed is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), so a late act reaches BREACH (both duties of the rule take the same input).
@ref s 206(1A) (src:19760-19765)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 206 act`
`s 206(1A) the public company must review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 206(1A) undertake a review of the fees, expenses and emoluments of the auditor to determine whether the independence of the auditor has been compromised`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE (PARTY Company `the name of the company`
           MUST `s 206(1A) send the outcome of the review to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company`
           WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send the outcome of the review of the auditor's fees to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings")
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not undertake the review of the auditor's fees, expenses and emoluments"

-- src:19767 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:19768 | and every director of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:19769 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:19770 | $5,000.
@ref s 206(2) (src:19767-19770)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 206` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 205(17) person charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206(2) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 206`
    THEN (CONSIDER person
          WHEN `s 205(17) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 205(17) any other person` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company and every director of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" names the persons it makes guilty (split site (i), fork line F-E1)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section" (an unmet element of the offence: split site (i), fork line F-E1)

@ref s 206(2) (src:19767-19770)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 206` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 205(17) person charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 206(2) the most the person may be fined on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 206(2) the person is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with section 206` person EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST 5000
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 207(1) and (1A): the auditor's report to the members, and to the directors`

-- (1): "An auditor of a company must report to the members -- (a) on the financial statements required to be laid before the company in general meeting and on the company's accounting and
-- other records relating to those financial statements; and (b) where the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are prepared, on the consolidated financial statements."
-- (1) gives the report no time of its own, but (1A) says of "a report by an auditor of a company under subsection (1)" that it must be furnished "in sufficient time", so the section's own standard of time governs it: the regulative rule below takes that period as an input (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), and the function says "in default" when a required report has not been made, as asked.
-- src:19775 | 207.—(1) An auditor of a company must report to the members —
-- src:19777 | (a) on the financial statements required to be laid before the
-- src:19778 | company in general meeting and on the company’s
-- src:19779 | accounting and other records relating to those financial
-- src:19780 | statements; and
-- src:19782 | (b) where the company is a parent company for which
-- src:19783 | consolidated financial statements are prepared, on the
-- src:19784 | consolidated financial statements.
@ref s 207(1) (src:19775-19784)
GIVEN `the auditor has reported to the members on the financial statements and the accounting and other records relating to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has reported to the members on the consolidated financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1) the auditor is in default of the duty to report to the members` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the auditor has reported to the members on the financial statements and the accounting and other records relating to them`) OR (`the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are prepared` AND (NOT `the auditor has reported to the members on the consolidated financial statements`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An auditor of a company must report to the members -- (a) on the financial statements ...; and (b) where the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are prepared, on the consolidated financial statements" (a duty met: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

@ref s 207(1) (src:19775-19784)
GIVEN `the name of the auditor` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("in sufficient time", given in s 207(1A) for a report under s 207(1)) allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 207 act`
`s 207(1) the auditor must report to the members` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor `the name of the auditor`
    MUST `s 207(1) report to the members`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "in sufficient time" (s 207(1A), of "a report by an auditor of a company under subsection (1)"); the period is an input, as found (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Auditor `the name of the auditor` BECAUSE "the auditor did not report to the members as section 207(1) requires"

-- (1A): "A report by an auditor of a company under subsection (1) must be furnished by the auditor to the directors of the company in sufficient time to enable the company to comply with the requirements of
-- section 203(1) in relation to that report but no offence is committed by an auditor under this subsection if the directors have not submitted the financial statements for audit as required under this Part in
-- sufficient time, having regard to the complexity of the financial statements, for the auditor to make the auditor's report."
-- src:19791 | (1A) A report by an auditor of a company under subsection (1) must
-- src:19792 | be furnished by the auditor to the directors of the company in
-- src:19793 | sufficient time to enable the company to comply with the
-- src:19794 | requirements of section 203(1) in relation to that report but no
-- src:19795 | offence is committed by an auditor under this subsection if the
-- src:19796 | directors have not submitted the financial statements for audit as
-- src:19797 | required under this Part in sufficient time, having regard to the
-- src:19798 | complexity of the financial statements, for the auditor to make the
-- src:19799 | auditor’s report.
@ref s 207(1A) (src:19791-19799)
GIVEN `the auditor furnished the report to the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was furnished in sufficient time to enable the company to comply with section 203(1) in relation to the report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1A) the auditor is in default of the duty to furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the auditor furnished the report to the directors` AND `it was furnished in sufficient time to enable the company to comply with section 203(1) in relation to the report`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A report by an auditor of a company under subsection (1) must be furnished by the auditor to the directors of the company in sufficient time to enable the company to comply with the requirements of section 203(1)" (a duty met: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

@ref s 207(1A) (src:19791-19799)
GIVEN `the directors submitted the financial statements for audit as required under this Part in sufficient time, having regard to the complexity of the financial statements, for the auditor to make the report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1A) the auditor commits no offence under the subsection` MEANS
    IF NOT `the directors submitted the financial statements for audit as required under this Part in sufficient time, having regard to the complexity of the financial statements, for the auditor to make the report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the directors did submit in sufficient time, the subsection does not say whether an offence is committed or what the penalty is; that is left to a provision outside the sources

-- "in sufficient time": no number of days in the text, so the section's own standard of time is the input `the period the standard of time allows, as found`, and a late act reaches BREACH (notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
@ref s 207(1A) (src:19791-19799)
GIVEN `the name of the auditor` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("in sufficient time") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 207 act`
`s 207(1A) the auditor must furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor `the name of the auditor`
    MUST `s 207(1A) furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "in sufficient time" (s 207(1A)); the period is an input, as found (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Auditor `the name of the auditor` BECAUSE "the auditor did not furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time to enable the company to comply with section 203(1)"

§ `Section 207(2): what the report must state`

-- (a): "whether the financial statements and, if the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are prepared, the consolidated financial statements are in the auditor's opinion
-- (i) in compliance with the requirements of the Accounting Standards; and (ii) give a true and fair view of (A) the financial position and performance of the company; and (B) if consolidated financial statements are required,
-- the financial position and performance of the group".
-- src:19803 | (2) An auditor must, in a report under this section, state —
-- src:19805 | (a) whether the financial statements and, if the company is a
-- src:19806 | parent company for which consolidated financial
-- src:19807 | statements are prepared, the consolidated financial
-- src:19808 | statements are in the auditor’s opinion —
-- src:19810 | (i) in compliance with the requirements of the
-- src:19811 | Accounting Standards; and
-- src:19813 | (ii) give a true and fair view of —
-- src:19815 | (A) the financial position and performance of the
-- src:19816 | company; and
-- src:19818 | (B) if consolidated financial statements are
-- src:19819 | required, the financial position and
-- src:19820 | performance of the group;
@ref s 207(2)(a) (src:19803-19820)
GIVEN `the report states whether the financial statements are in compliance with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether the financial statements give a true and fair view of the financial position and performance of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether the consolidated financial statements are in compliance with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether the consolidated financial statements give a true and fair view of the financial position and performance of the group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(2)(a) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the opinions on the financial statements` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the report states whether the financial statements are in compliance with the requirements of the Accounting Standards`
            AND `the report states whether the financial statements give a true and fair view of the financial position and performance of the company`
            AND ((NOT `the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are prepared`)
                 OR (    `the report states whether the consolidated financial statements are in compliance with the requirements of the Accounting Standards`
                     AND `the report states whether the consolidated financial statements give a true and fair view of the financial position and performance of the group`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An auditor must, in a report under this section, state -- (a) whether the financial statements and, if the company is a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are prepared, the consolidated financial statements are in the auditor's opinion ..." (a duty met: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

-- (aa): the text prints the label "(aa)" twice: the first block states the condition ("if the financial statements ... do not comply with any requirement of the Accounting Standards and the non-compliance is neither
-- (i) approved by the Registrar under section 201(12); nor (ii) allowed under an order by the Minister under section 201(15A)") and the second states what is to be stated ("whether the non-compliance is, in the opinion of the auditor,
-- necessary for the financial statements ... to give a true and fair view of any matter required by section 201 to be dealt with in them"). Read as one paragraph, a condition and its consequence (finding in NOTES.md).
-- src:19822 | (aa) if the financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:19823 | statements do not comply with any requirement of the
-- src:19824 | Accounting Standards and the non‑compliance is
-- src:19825 | neither —
-- src:19827 | (i) approved by the Registrar under section 201(12); nor
-- src:19829 | (ii) allowed under an order by the Minister under
-- src:19830 | section 201(15A),
-- src:19832 | (aa) whether the non‑compliance is, in the opinion of the
-- src:19833 | auditor, necessary for the financial statements or
-- src:19834 | consolidated financial statements to give a true and fair
-- src:19839 | view of any matter required by section 201 to be dealt with
-- src:19840 | in them;
@ref s 207(2)(aa) (src:19822-19840)
GIVEN `the financial statements or consolidated financial statements do not comply with a requirement of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the non-compliance is approved by the Registrar under section 201(12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the non-compliance is allowed under an order by the Minister under section 201(15A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether the non-compliance is, in the opinion of the auditor, necessary for the statements to give a true and fair view of any matter required by section 201 to be dealt with in them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(2)(aa) the auditor is in default of the duty to state whether the non-compliance is necessary for a true and fair view` MEANS
    IF     `the financial statements or consolidated financial statements do not comply with a requirement of the Accounting Standards`
       AND (NOT `the non-compliance is approved by the Registrar under section 201(12)`)
       AND (NOT `the non-compliance is allowed under an order by the Minister under section 201(15A)`)
       AND (NOT `the report states whether the non-compliance is, in the opinion of the auditor, necessary for the statements to give a true and fair view of any matter required by section 201 to be dealt with in them`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(aa) if the financial statements or consolidated financial statements do not comply with any requirement of the Accounting Standards and the non-compliance is neither (i) approved by the Registrar under section 201(12); nor (ii) allowed under an order by the Minister under section 201(15A), (aa) whether the non-compliance is, in the opinion of the auditor, necessary for the financial statements ... to give a true and fair view" (a duty met, or its "if" not met: fork line F-D1)

-- src:19844 | (b) whether the accounting and other records required by this
-- src:19845 | Act to be kept by the company and, if it is a parent
-- src:19846 | company, by the subsidiary corporations other than those
-- src:19847 | of which the auditor has not acted as auditor have been, in
-- src:19848 | the auditor’s opinion, properly kept in accordance with this
-- src:19849 | Act;
@ref s 207(2)(b) (src:19844-19849)
GIVEN `the report states whether the accounting and other records required by this Act to be kept by the company and, if it is a parent company, by the subsidiary corporations other than those of which the auditor has not acted as auditor have been, in the auditor's opinion, properly kept in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(2)(b) the auditor is in default of the duty to state whether the records have been properly kept` MEANS
    IF NOT `the report states whether the accounting and other records required by this Act to be kept by the company and, if it is a parent company, by the subsidiary corporations other than those of which the auditor has not acted as auditor have been, in the auditor's opinion, properly kept in accordance with this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) whether the accounting and other records required by this Act to be kept by the company and, if it is a parent company, by the subsidiary corporations ... have been, in the auditor's opinion, properly kept in accordance with this Act" (a duty met: fork line F-D1)

-- src:19853 | (d) any defect or irregularity in the financial statements or
-- src:19854 | consolidated financial statements and any matter not set
-- src:19855 | out in the financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:19856 | statements without regard to which a true and fair view of
-- src:19857 | the matters dealt with by the financial statements or
-- src:19858 | consolidated financial statements would not be obtained;
-- src:19859 | and
@ref s 207(2)(d) (src:19853-19859)
GIVEN `there is a defect or irregularity in the financial statements or consolidated financial statements, or a matter not set out in them, without regard to which a true and fair view of the matters they deal with would not be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(2)(d) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the defect, irregularity or matter` MEANS
    IF `there is a defect or irregularity in the financial statements or consolidated financial statements, or a matter not set out in them, without regard to which a true and fair view of the matters they deal with would not be obtained` AND (NOT `the report states it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) any defect or irregularity in the financial statements or consolidated financial statements and any matter not set out in the financial statements or consolidated financial statements without regard to which a true and fair view of the matters dealt with by the financial statements or consolidated financial statements would not be obtained" (a duty met, or none to state: fork line F-D1)

-- src:19861 | (e) if the auditor is not satisfied as to any matter referred to in
-- src:19862 | paragraph (a), (aa) or (b), the auditor’s reasons for not
-- src:19863 | being so satisfied.
@ref s 207(2)(e) (src:19861-19863)
GIVEN `the auditor is not satisfied as to a matter referred to in paragraph (a), (aa) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the auditor's reasons for not being so satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(2)(e) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the reasons for not being satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the auditor is not satisfied as to a matter referred to in paragraph (a), (aa) or (b)` AND (NOT `the report states the auditor's reasons for not being so satisfied`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) if the auditor is not satisfied as to any matter referred to in paragraph (a), (aa) or (b), the auditor's reasons for not being so satisfied" (a duty met, or its "if" not met: fork line F-D1)

§ `Section 207(3) and (4): the duty to form opinions`

-- (3): "It is the duty of an auditor of a company to form an opinion as to each of the following matters: (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) [Deleted by Act 36 of 2014]; (e) where consolidated financial statements are prepared
-- otherwise than as one set of consolidated financial statements for the group, whether the auditor agrees with the reasons ...".
-- src:19867 | (3) It is the duty of an auditor of a company to form an opinion as to
-- src:19868 | each of the following matters:
-- src:19870 | (a) whether the auditor has obtained all the information and
-- src:19871 | explanations that the auditor required;
-- src:19873 | (b) whether proper accounting and other records, excluding
-- src:19874 | registers, required to be kept under section 199(1), have
-- src:19875 | been kept by the company as required by this Act;
-- src:19877 | (c) whether the returns received from branch offices of the
-- src:19878 | company are adequate;
-- src:19880 | (d) [Deleted by Act 36 of 2014]
-- src:19882 | (e) where consolidated financial statements are prepared
-- src:19883 | otherwise than as one set of consolidated financial
-- src:19884 | statements for the group, whether the auditor agrees with
-- src:19885 | the reasons for preparing them in the form in which they
-- src:19890 | are prepared, as given by the directors in the financial
-- src:19891 | statements,
@ref s 207(3) (src:19867-19891)
GIVEN `the auditor has formed an opinion on whether the auditor has obtained all the information and explanations that the auditor required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has formed an opinion on whether proper accounting and other records, excluding registers, required to be kept under section 199(1), have been kept by the company as required by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has formed an opinion on whether the returns received from branch offices of the company are adequate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `consolidated financial statements are prepared otherwise than as one set of consolidated financial statements for the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has formed an opinion on whether the auditor agrees with the reasons for preparing them in the form in which they are prepared, as given by the directors in the financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to form an opinion on each of the matters` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the auditor has formed an opinion on whether the auditor has obtained all the information and explanations that the auditor required`
            AND `the auditor has formed an opinion on whether proper accounting and other records, excluding registers, required to be kept under section 199(1), have been kept by the company as required by this Act`
            AND `the auditor has formed an opinion on whether the returns received from branch offices of the company are adequate`
            AND ((NOT `consolidated financial statements are prepared otherwise than as one set of consolidated financial statements for the group`)
                 OR `the auditor has formed an opinion on whether the auditor agrees with the reasons for preparing them in the form in which they are prepared, as given by the directors in the financial statements`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is the duty of an auditor of a company to form an opinion as to each of the following matters" (a duty met: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

-- src:19893 | and the auditor must state in the auditor’s report particulars of any
-- src:19894 | deficiency, failure or shortcoming in respect of any matter referred to
-- src:19895 | in this subsection.
@ref s 207(3) (src:19893-19895)
GIVEN `there is a deficiency, failure or shortcoming in respect of a matter referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor states particulars of it in the auditor's report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to state particulars of a deficiency, failure or shortcoming` MEANS
    IF `there is a deficiency, failure or shortcoming in respect of a matter referred to in subsection (3)` AND (NOT `the auditor states particulars of it in the auditor's report`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the auditor must state in the auditor's report particulars of any deficiency, failure or shortcoming in respect of any matter referred to in this subsection" (a duty met, or none to state: fork line F-D1)

-- (4): "An auditor is not required to form an opinion in the auditor's report as to whether the accounting and other records of subsidiary corporations (which are not incorporated in Singapore) of a Singapore parent company
-- have been kept in accordance with this Act." A flat negative, within the scope it names.
-- src:19899 | (4) An auditor is not required to form an opinion in the auditor’s
-- src:19900 | report as to whether the accounting and other records of subsidiary
-- src:19901 | corporations (which are not incorporated in Singapore) of a
-- src:19902 | Singapore parent company have been kept in accordance with this
-- src:19903 | Act.
@ref s 207(4) (src:19899-19903)
GIVEN `the subsidiary corporation is not incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent company is a Singapore company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(4) the auditor is not required to form an opinion on whether the records of the subsidiary corporation have been kept in accordance with this Act` MEANS
    IF `the subsidiary corporation is not incorporated in Singapore` AND `the parent company is a Singapore company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subsidiary corporations (which are not incorporated in Singapore) of a Singapore parent company" is a scope limit with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)); the text says nothing of another subsidiary corporation

§ `Section 207(5), (6) and (11): the auditor's access and the right to require information`

-- (11): "The reference to the registers of -- (a) a company in subsection (5); (b) a subsidiary corporation of a parent company in subsection (6); or (c) a corporation in subsection (10), does not include any register
-- kept by the company, subsidiary corporation of a parent company or corporation (as the case may be) under Part 11A." A flat negative for that one kind of register.
-- src:20034 | (11) The reference to the registers of —
-- src:20036 | (a) a company in subsection (5);
-- src:20041 | (b) a subsidiary corporation of a parent company in
-- src:20042 | subsection (6); or
-- src:20044 | (c) a corporation in subsection (10),
-- src:20046 | does not include any register kept by the company, subsidiary
-- src:20047 | corporation of a parent company or corporation (as the case may be)
-- src:20048 | under Part 11A.
@ref s 207(11) (src:20034-20048)
GIVEN item IS A `s 207(5) access item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(11) the item is excluded from the reference to registers in subsections (5), (6) and (10)` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
        WHEN `s 207(5) a register kept under Part 11A` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 207(5) a register other than a register kept under Part 11A` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (11) takes out only a register kept under Part 11A; whether another register is within subsections (5), (6) and (10) is for those subsections
        WHEN `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (11) speaks of registers only

-- (5): "An auditor of a company has a right of access at all times to the accounting and other records, including registers, of the company".
-- A person who is not an auditor of the company: the subsection is silent (scope limit with no "only": NOTHING).
-- src:19907 | (5) An auditor of a company has a right of access at all times to the
-- src:19908 | accounting and other records, including registers, of the company,
-- src:19909 | and is entitled to require from any officer of the company and any
-- src:19910 | auditor of a company that is deemed to be related to the company by
-- src:19911 | virtue of section 6 such information and explanations as the auditor
-- src:19912 | desires for the purposes of audit.
@ref s 207(5) (src:19907-19912)
GIVEN `the person is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS A `s 207(5) access item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(5) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item` MEANS
    IF `the person is an auditor of the company`
    THEN (IF `s 207(11) the item is excluded from the reference to registers in subsections (5), (6) and (10)` item EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include any register kept by the company ... under Part 11A" (subsection (11): a flat negative)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor of a company has a right of access" is a scope limit with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

-- (5), second limb: the auditor "is entitled to require from any officer of the company and any auditor of a company that is deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6 such information and explanations as the
-- auditor desires for the purposes of audit". The relation of section 6 is the keel's (`s 6 the corporations are deemed to be related to each other`): asked as its three limbs.
-- An "entitled"-named function the Guide does not settle (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 3: fork line F-N1); it answers JUST TRUE or NOTHING only, never JUST FALSE.
@ref s 207(5) (src:19907-19912)
GIVEN `the person asking is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 207(5) person asked`
      `the company is the holding company of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a subsidiary of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a subsidiary of the holding company of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are information and explanations that the auditor desires for the purposes of audit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(5) the auditor is entitled to require information and explanations from the person` MEANS
    IF `the person asking is an auditor of the company` AND `they are information and explanations that the auditor desires for the purposes of audit`
    THEN (CONSIDER person
          WHEN `s 207(5) an officer of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 207(5) an auditor of another company` THEN
              (IF `s 6 the corporations are deemed to be related to each other` `the company is the holding company of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` `the company is a subsidiary of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` `the company is a subsidiary of the holding company of the corporation of which the person asked is the auditor` EQUALS JUST TRUE
               THEN JUST TRUE
               ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any auditor of a company that is deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6" is a scope limit with no "only"; the text says nothing of an auditor of a company that is not so related
          WHEN `s 207(5) any other person` THEN NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names an officer of the company and an auditor of a related company; of any other person it says nothing
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor of a company ... is entitled to require ... such information and explanations as the auditor desires for the purposes of audit" (an entitlement limited to the auditor and to what the auditor desires for the audit)

-- (6): "An auditor of a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required has a right of access at all times to the accounting and other records, including registers, of any subsidiary corporation,
-- and is entitled to require from any officer or auditor of any subsidiary corporation, at the expense of the parent company, such information and explanations in relation to the affairs of the subsidiary corporation as the auditor
-- requires for the purpose of reporting on the consolidated financial statements."
-- src:19916 | (6) An auditor of a parent company for which consolidated
-- src:19917 | financial statements are required has a right of access at all times
-- src:19918 | to the accounting and other records, including registers, of any
-- src:19919 | subsidiary corporation, and is entitled to require from any officer or
-- src:19920 | auditor of any subsidiary corporation, at the expense of the parent
-- src:19921 | company, such information and explanations in relation to the affairs
-- src:19922 | of the subsidiary corporation as the auditor requires for the purpose of
-- src:19923 | reporting on the consolidated financial statements.
@ref s 207(6) (src:19916-19923)
GIVEN `the person is an auditor of a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS A `s 207(5) access item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(6) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item of the subsidiary corporation` MEANS
    IF `the person is an auditor of a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required`
    THEN (IF `s 207(11) the item is excluded from the reference to registers in subsections (5), (6) and (10)` item EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include any register kept by ... subsidiary corporation of a parent company ... under Part 11A" (subsection (11): a flat negative)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor of a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required has a right of access" is a scope limit with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

@ref s 207(6) (src:19916-19923)
GIVEN `the person asking is an auditor of a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 207(6) person asked`
      `they are information and explanations in relation to the affairs of the subsidiary corporation that the auditor requires for the purpose of reporting on the consolidated financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(6) the auditor is entitled, at the expense of the parent company, to require information and explanations from the person` MEANS
    IF `the person asking is an auditor of a parent company for which consolidated financial statements are required` AND `they are information and explanations in relation to the affairs of the subsidiary corporation that the auditor requires for the purpose of reporting on the consolidated financial statements`
    THEN (CONSIDER person
          WHEN `s 207(6) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 207(6) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 207(6) any other person` THEN NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names any officer or auditor of any subsidiary corporation; of any other person it says nothing
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor of a parent company ... is entitled to require ... such information and explanations ... as the auditor requires for the purpose of reporting on the consolidated financial statements" (an entitlement limited to that auditor and that purpose)

§ `Section 207(7) and (8): the report attached and read, and the auditor at the meeting`

-- (7): "The auditor's report must be attached to or endorsed on the financial statements or consolidated financial statements and must, if any member so requires, be read before the company in general meeting and must be
-- open to inspection by any member at any reasonable time." The text names no one who must do these things, so no regulative rule is written: only a decision function.
-- src:19927 | (7) The auditor’s report must be attached to or endorsed on the
-- src:19928 | financial statements or consolidated financial statements and must, if
-- src:19929 | any member so requires, be read before the company in general
-- src:19930 | meeting and must be open to inspection by any member at any
-- src:19931 | reasonable time.
@ref s 207(7) (src:19927-19931)
GIVEN `the report is attached to or endorsed on the financial statements or consolidated financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member has required the report to be read before the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report has been read before the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is open to inspection by any member at any reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(7) the report is attached or endorsed, read on a member's request and open to inspection as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `the report is attached to or endorsed on the financial statements or consolidated financial statements`
       AND ((NOT `a member has required the report to be read before the company in general meeting`) OR `the report has been read before the company in general meeting`)
       AND `the report is open to inspection by any member at any reasonable time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The auditor's report must be attached to or endorsed on the financial statements or consolidated financial statements and must, if any member so requires, be read before the company in general meeting and must be open to inspection by any member at any reasonable time" (a demand met: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

-- (8): "An auditor of a company or an agent authorised by the auditor in writing for the purpose is entitled to attend any general meeting of the company and to receive all notices of, and other communications relating to,
-- any general meeting which a member is entitled to receive, and to be heard at any general meeting which the auditor attends on any part of the business of the meeting which concerns the auditor in such capacity as auditor."
-- "Entitled"-named functions the Guide does not settle (fork line F-N1); each answers JUST TRUE or NOTHING only. Whether an agent may be heard when the auditor does not attend is read in favour of the agent (fork line F-A1).
-- src:19935 | (8) An auditor of a company or an agent authorised by the auditor in
-- src:19936 | writing for the purpose is entitled to attend any general meeting of the
-- src:19937 | company and to receive all notices of, and other communications
-- src:19942 | relating to, any general meeting which a member is entitled to
-- src:19943 | receive, and to be heard at any general meeting which the auditor
-- src:19944 | attends on any part of the business of the meeting which concerns the
-- src:19945 | auditor in such capacity as auditor.
@ref s 207(8) (src:19935-19945)
GIVEN person IS A `s 207(8) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(8) the person is entitled to attend any general meeting of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
        WHEN `s 207(8) an auditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 207(8) an agent authorised by the auditor in writing for the purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 207(8) any other person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor of a company or an agent authorised by the auditor in writing for the purpose is entitled" is a scope limit with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

@ref s 207(8) (src:19935-19945)
GIVEN person IS A `s 207(8) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(8) the person is entitled to receive all notices of, and other communications relating to, any general meeting which a member is entitled to receive` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
        WHEN `s 207(8) an auditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 207(8) an agent authorised by the auditor in writing for the purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 207(8) any other person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): as above

@ref s 207(8) (src:19935-19945)
GIVEN person IS A `s 207(8) person`
      `the person attends the general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the business concerns the auditor in the capacity of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(8) the person is entitled to be heard at the general meeting on the part of the business` MEANS
    IF `the person attends the general meeting` AND `the part of the business concerns the auditor in the capacity of auditor`
    THEN (CONSIDER person
          WHEN `s 207(8) an auditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 207(8) an agent authorised by the auditor in writing for the purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 207(8) any other person` THEN NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): as above
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to be heard at any general meeting which the auditor attends on any part of the business of the meeting which concerns the auditor in such capacity as auditor" limits the grant to a meeting attended and business that concerns the auditor as auditor

§ `Section 207(9) to (9D): reporting a breach, and a serious offence`

-- (9): "If an auditor, in the course of the performance of such duties as auditor of a company, is satisfied that -- (a) there has been a breach or non-observance of any of the provisions of this Act; and (b) the circumstances are such that
-- in the auditor's opinion the matter has not been or will not be adequately dealt with by comment in the auditor's report ... or by bringing the matter to the notice of the directors ..., the auditor must immediately report the matter in writing to the Registrar."
-- src:19947 | (9) If an auditor, in the course of the performance of such duties as
-- src:19948 | auditor of a company, is satisfied that —
-- src:19950 | (a) there has been a breach or non‑observance of any of the
-- src:19951 | provisions of this Act; and
-- src:19953 | (b) the circumstances are such that in the auditor’s opinion the
-- src:19954 | matter has not been or will not be adequately dealt with by
-- src:19955 | comment in the auditor’s report on the financial statements
-- src:19956 | or consolidated financial statements or by bringing the
-- src:19957 | matter to the notice of the directors of the company or, if
-- src:19958 | the company is a subsidiary company, of the directors of
-- src:19959 | the parent company,
-- src:19961 | the auditor must immediately report the matter in writing to the
-- src:19962 | Registrar.
@ref s 207(9) (src:19947-19962)
GIVEN `the auditor is satisfied that there has been a breach or non-observance of a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the auditor's opinion the matter has not been or will not be adequately dealt with by comment in the auditor's report or by bringing it to the notice of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has reported the matter in writing to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(9) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF     `the auditor is satisfied that there has been a breach or non-observance of a provision of this Act`
       AND `in the auditor's opinion the matter has not been or will not be adequately dealt with by comment in the auditor's report or by bringing it to the notice of the directors`
       AND (NOT (`the auditor has reported the matter in writing to the Registrar` AND `the auditor did so immediately`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an auditor ... is satisfied that -- (a) there has been a breach or non-observance of any of the provisions of this Act; and (b) the circumstances are such that ..., the auditor must immediately report the matter in writing to the Registrar" (a duty met, or its "if" not met: fork line F-D1)

-- "immediately": no number of days: the section's own standard of time is the input `the period the standard of time allows, as found`, so a late act reaches BREACH (notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
@ref s 207(9) (src:19947-19962)
GIVEN `the name of the auditor` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("immediately") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 207 act`
`s 207(9) the auditor must report the matter in writing to the Registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor `the name of the auditor`
    MUST `s 207(9) report the matter in writing to the Registrar`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "immediately" (s 207(9)); the period is an input, as found (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Auditor `the name of the auditor` BECAUSE "the auditor did not report the breach or non-observance in writing to the Registrar"

-- (9D): "In subsection (9A), 'a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty' means -- (a) an offence that is punishable by imprisonment for a term that is not less than 2 years; and
-- (b) the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained from the commission of such an offence is not less than $100,000." Read: the longest term the offence is punishable with is at least 2 years (fork line F-J1).
-- src:19994 | (9D) In subsection (9A), “a serious offence involving fraud or
-- src:19995 | dishonesty” means —
-- src:19997 | (a) an offence that is punishable by imprisonment for a term
-- src:19998 | that is not less than 2 years; and
-- src:20000 | (b) the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained
-- src:20001 | from the commission of such an offence is not less than
-- src:20002 | $100,000.
@ref s 207(9D) (src:19994-20002)
GIVEN `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained from the commission of the offence, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(9D) the offence is a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty` MEANS
    IF `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in years` AT LEAST 2 AND `the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained from the commission of the offence, in Singapore dollars` AT LEAST 100000
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty' means -- (a) an offence that is punishable by imprisonment for a term that is not less than 2 years; and (b) the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained from the commission of such an offence is not less than $100,000" (a "means" definition)

-- (9C): "An auditor who is under a legal duty under any other written law to make a report to the Monetary Authority of Singapore in relation to an offence involving fraud or dishonesty ..., is not required to make a report
-- to the Minister under subsection (9A) if the auditor has already made a report in relation to the same offence under that written law to the Monetary Authority of Singapore."
-- src:19981 | (9C) An auditor who is under a legal duty under any other written
-- src:19982 | law to make a report to the Monetary Authority of Singapore in
-- src:19983 | relation to an offence involving fraud or dishonesty that the auditor
-- src:19984 | becomes aware of in the course of the performance of the auditor’s
-- src:19985 | duties as such, is not required to make a report to the Minister under
-- src:19986 | subsection (9A) if the auditor has already made a report in relation to
-- src:19991 | the same offence under that written law to the Monetary Authority of
-- src:19992 | Singapore.
@ref s 207(9C) (src:19981-19992)
GIVEN `the auditor is under a legal duty under another written law to make a report to the Monetary Authority of Singapore in relation to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has already made a report in relation to the same offence under that written law to the Monetary Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(9C) the auditor is not required to make a report to the Minister under subsection (9A)` MEANS
    IF `the auditor is under a legal duty under another written law to make a report to the Monetary Authority of Singapore in relation to the offence` AND `the auditor has already made a report in relation to the same offence under that written law to the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is not required to make a report to the Minister under subsection (9A) if the auditor has already made a report ..." gives the relief on that condition and says nothing of an auditor who has not made that report (subsection (9A) answers)

-- (9A): "Despite subsection (9), if an auditor of a public company or a subsidiary corporation of a public company, in the course of the performance of the auditor's duties as such, has reason to believe that a serious offence
-- involving fraud or dishonesty is being or has been committed against the company by officers or employees of the company, the auditor must immediately report the matter to the Minister."
-- src:19966 | (9A) Despite subsection (9), if an auditor of a public company or a
-- src:19967 | subsidiary corporation of a public company, in the course of the
-- src:19968 | performance of the auditor’s duties as such, has reason to believe that
-- src:19969 | a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty is being or has been
-- src:19970 | committed against the company by officers or employees of the
-- src:19971 | company, the auditor must immediately report the matter to the
-- src:19972 | Minister.
@ref s 207(9A) (src:19966-19972)
GIVEN `the auditor is an auditor of a public company or of a subsidiary corporation of a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has reason to believe that an offence is being or has been committed against the company by officers or employees of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained from the commission of the offence, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the auditor is not required to make a report to the Minister because of section 207(9C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has reported the matter to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor did so immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` MEANS
    IF     `the auditor is an auditor of a public company or of a subsidiary corporation of a public company`
       AND `the auditor has reason to believe that an offence is being or has been committed against the company by officers or employees of the company`
       AND `s 207(9D) the offence is a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty` `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in years` `the value of the property obtained or likely to be obtained from the commission of the offence, in Singapore dollars` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (NOT `the auditor is not required to make a report to the Minister because of section 207(9C)`)
       AND (NOT (`the auditor has reported the matter to the Minister` AND `the auditor did so immediately`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if an auditor of a public company or a subsidiary corporation of a public company ... has reason to believe that a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty is being or has been committed against the company by officers or employees of the company, the auditor must immediately report the matter to the Minister" (a duty met, or its "if" not met: fork line F-D1)

-- "immediately": no number of days: the section's own standard of time is the input `the period the standard of time allows, as found`, so a late act reaches BREACH (notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
@ref s 207(9A) (src:19966-19972)
GIVEN `the name of the auditor` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("immediately") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 207 act`
`s 207(9A) the auditor must report the matter to the Minister` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor `the name of the auditor`
    MUST `s 207(9A) report the matter to the Minister`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "immediately" (s 207(9A)); the period is an input, as found (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Auditor `the name of the auditor` BECAUSE "the auditor did not report the serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty to the Minister"

-- (9B): "No duty to which an auditor of a company may be subject is to be regarded as having been contravened by reason of the auditor reporting the matter mentioned in subsection (9A) in good faith to the Minister."
-- src:19976 | (9B) No duty to which an auditor of a company may be subject is to
-- src:19977 | be regarded as having been contravened by reason of the auditor
-- src:19978 | reporting the matter mentioned in subsection (9A) in good faith to the
-- src:19979 | Minister.
@ref s 207(9B) (src:19976-19979)
GIVEN `the auditor reported the matter mentioned in subsection (9A) to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor did so in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(9B) no duty to which the auditor is subject is regarded as contravened by the report` MEANS
    IF `the auditor reported the matter mentioned in subsection (9A) to the Minister` AND `the auditor did so in good faith`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason of the auditor reporting the matter mentioned in subsection (9A) in good faith to the Minister" protects a report so made and says nothing of a report not made in good faith

§ `Section 207(10): the offences`

-- (10): "The following persons are guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $4,000: (a) any officer of a company who refuses or fails without lawful excuse to allow an auditor of the company
-- access, in accordance with subsection (5), ...; (b) any officer or auditor of a subsidiary corporation who refuses or fails without lawful excuse to allow an auditor of its parent company access, in accordance with subsection (6), ...;
-- (c) any officer of a company or officer or auditor of a subsidiary corporation who refuses or fails without lawful excuse to give any information or explanation as and when required under subsection (5) or (6);
-- (d) any officer of a company or any officer or auditor of a subsidiary corporation who otherwise hinders, obstructs or delays an auditor ...". Paragraphs (a) to (c) carry "without lawful excuse"; paragraph (d) does not.
-- The access refused is read through subsection (11): a register kept under Part 11A is not one the refusal of which is an offence.
-- An unmet element of an offence: JUST FALSE (split site (i), fork line F-E1).
-- src:20006 | (10) The following persons are guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:20007 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $4,000:
-- src:20009 | (a) any officer of a company who refuses or fails without
-- src:20010 | lawful excuse to allow an auditor of the company access, in
-- src:20011 | accordance with subsection (5), to any accounting and
-- src:20012 | other records, including registers, of the company in the
-- src:20013 | officer’s custody or control;
-- src:20015 | (b) any officer or auditor of a subsidiary corporation who
-- src:20016 | refuses or fails without lawful excuse to allow an auditor of
-- src:20017 | its parent company access, in accordance with
-- src:20018 | subsection (6), to any accounting and other records,
-- src:20019 | including registers, of the subsidiary corporation in the
-- src:20020 | officer’s or auditor’s custody or control;
-- src:20022 | (c) any officer of a company or officer or auditor of a
-- src:20023 | subsidiary corporation who refuses or fails without lawful
-- src:20024 | excuse to give any information or explanation as and when
-- src:20025 | required under subsection (5) or (6);
-- src:20027 | (d) any officer of a company or any officer or auditor of a
-- src:20028 | subsidiary corporation who otherwise hinders, obstructs or
-- src:20029 | delays an auditor in the performance of the auditor’s duties
-- src:20030 | or the exercise of the auditor’s powers under this section.
@ref s 207(10) (src:20006-20030)
GIVEN person IS A `s 207(10) person`
      conduct IS A `s 207(10) conduct`
      `the person had lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS A `s 207(5) access item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER conduct
        WHEN `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` THEN
            (IF     (CONSIDER person
                     WHEN `s 207(10) an officer of a company` THEN TRUE
                     WHEN `s 207(10) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` THEN FALSE
                     WHEN `s 207(10) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation` THEN FALSE
                     WHEN `s 207(10) any other person` THEN FALSE)
                AND (NOT `the person had lawful excuse`)
                AND (NOT (`s 207(11) the item is excluded from the reference to registers in subsections (5), (6) and (10)` item EQUALS JUST TRUE))
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) any officer of a company who refuses or fails without lawful excuse to allow an auditor of the company access, in accordance with subsection (5), to any accounting and other records, including registers" (an unmet element of the offence: split site (i), fork line F-E1; a register kept under Part 11A: subsection (11))
        WHEN `s 207(10)(b) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the parent company access in accordance with subsection (6)` THEN
            (IF     (CONSIDER person
                     WHEN `s 207(10) an officer of a company` THEN FALSE
                     WHEN `s 207(10) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` THEN TRUE
                     WHEN `s 207(10) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation` THEN TRUE
                     WHEN `s 207(10) any other person` THEN FALSE)
                AND (NOT `the person had lawful excuse`)
                AND (NOT (`s 207(11) the item is excluded from the reference to registers in subsections (5), (6) and (10)` item EQUALS JUST TRUE))
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) any officer or auditor of a subsidiary corporation who refuses or fails without lawful excuse to allow an auditor of its parent company access, in accordance with subsection (6)" (an unmet element of the offence: split site (i), fork line F-E1)
        WHEN `s 207(10)(c) refused or failed to give information or explanation as and when required under subsection (5) or (6)` THEN
            (IF     (CONSIDER person
                     WHEN `s 207(10) an officer of a company` THEN TRUE
                     WHEN `s 207(10) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` THEN TRUE
                     WHEN `s 207(10) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation` THEN TRUE
                     WHEN `s 207(10) any other person` THEN FALSE)
                AND (NOT `the person had lawful excuse`)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) any officer of a company or officer or auditor of a subsidiary corporation who refuses or fails without lawful excuse to give any information or explanation as and when required under subsection (5) or (6)" (an unmet element of the offence: split site (i), fork line F-E1)
        WHEN `s 207(10)(d) otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed an auditor in the performance of the auditor's duties or the exercise of the auditor's powers under section 207` THEN
            (IF (CONSIDER person
                 WHEN `s 207(10) an officer of a company` THEN TRUE
                 WHEN `s 207(10) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` THEN TRUE
                 WHEN `s 207(10) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation` THEN TRUE
                 WHEN `s 207(10) any other person` THEN FALSE)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) any officer of a company or any officer or auditor of a subsidiary corporation who otherwise hinders, obstructs or delays an auditor in the performance of the auditor's duties or the exercise of the auditor's powers under this section" (an unmet element of the offence: split site (i), fork line F-E1)

@ref s 207(10) (src:20006-20030)
GIVEN person IS A `s 207(10) person`
      conduct IS A `s 207(10) conduct`
      `the person had lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS A `s 207(5) access item`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 207(10) the most the person may be fined on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` person conduct `the person had lawful excuse` item EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST 4000
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the persons it makes guilty

§ `Section 208: qualified privilege`

-- (1): "An auditor shall not, in the absence of malice on the auditor's part, be liable to any action for defamation at the suit of any person in respect of any statement which the auditor makes in the course of the auditor's
-- duties as such, whether the statement is made orally or in writing." A protection limited by its own wording ("in the absence of malice"): with malice the text is silent: NOTHING.
-- src:20055 | 208.—(1) An auditor shall not, in the absence of malice on the
-- src:20056 | auditor’s part, be liable to any action for defamation at the suit of any
-- src:20057 | person in respect of any statement which the auditor makes in the
-- src:20058 | course of the auditor’s duties as such, whether the statement is made
-- src:20059 | orally or in writing.
@ref s 208(1) (src:20055-20059)
GIVEN `the statement is one which the auditor makes in the course of the auditor's duties as such, whether orally or in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is malice on the auditor's part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 208(1) the auditor is not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the statement` MEANS
    IF `the statement is one which the auditor makes in the course of the auditor's duties as such, whether orally or in writing` AND (NOT `there is malice on the auditor's part`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor shall not, in the absence of malice on the auditor's part, be liable to any action for defamation ... in respect of any statement which the auditor makes in the course of the auditor's duties as such" protects that statement in the absence of malice and says nothing of liability otherwise (the grant rule of 2026-11-12)

-- (2): "A person shall not, in the absence of malice on the person's part, be liable to any action for defamation at the suit of any person in respect of the publication of any document prepared by an auditor in the course of the
-- auditor's duties and required by this Act to be lodged with the Registrar."
-- src:20061 | (2) A person shall not, in the absence of malice on the person’s part,
-- src:20062 | be liable to any action for defamation at the suit of any person in
-- src:20063 | respect of the publication of any document prepared by an auditor in
-- src:20064 | the course of the auditor’s duties and required by this Act to be lodged
-- src:20065 | with the Registrar.
@ref s 208(2) (src:20061-20065)
GIVEN `the document was prepared by an auditor in the course of the auditor's duties and is required by this Act to be lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is malice on the part of the person who published it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 208(2) the person is not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the publication of the document` MEANS
    IF `the document was prepared by an auditor in the course of the auditor's duties and is required by this Act to be lodged with the Registrar` AND (NOT `there is malice on the part of the person who published it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person shall not, in the absence of malice on the person's part, be liable to any action for defamation ... in respect of the publication of any document prepared by an auditor in the course of the auditor's duties and required by this Act to be lodged with the Registrar" protects that publication in the absence of malice and says nothing of liability otherwise (the grant rule of 2026-11-12)

-- (3): "This section does not limit or affect any other right, privilege or immunity that an auditor or other person has as defendant in an action for defamation."
-- src:20067 | (3) This section does not limit or affect any other right, privilege or
-- src:20068 | immunity that an auditor or other person has as defendant in an action
-- src:20069 | for defamation.
@ref s 208(3) (src:20067-20069)
GIVEN `the right, privilege or immunity is one that an auditor or other person has as defendant in an action for defamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 208(3) section 208 limits or affects the right, privilege or immunity` MEANS
    IF `the right, privilege or immunity is one that an auditor or other person has as defendant in an action for defamation`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not limit or affect any other right, privilege or immunity that an auditor or other person has as defendant in an action for defamation" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a right, privilege or immunity as defendant in an action for defamation

§ `Section 208A: provisions indemnifying auditors`

-- (1): "Any provision, whether in the constitution or in any contract with a company or otherwise, for exempting any auditor of the company from, or indemnifying the auditor against, any liability which by law would
-- otherwise attach to the auditor in respect of any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust of which the auditor may be guilty in relation to the company is void."
-- A provision outside that description: the subsection is silent (a scope limit with no "only": NOTHING).
-- src:20073 | 208A.—(1) Any provision, whether in the constitution or in any
-- src:20074 | contract with a company or otherwise, for exempting any auditor of
-- src:20075 | the company from, or indemnifying the auditor against, any liability
-- src:20076 | which by law would otherwise attach to the auditor in respect of any
-- src:20077 | negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust of which the
-- src:20078 | auditor may be guilty in relation to the company is void.
@ref s 208A(1) (src:20073-20078)
GIVEN `the provision exempts the auditor of the company from, or indemnifies the auditor against, a liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is one which by law would otherwise attach to the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust of which the auditor may be guilty in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 208A(1) the provision is void` MEANS
    IF     `the provision exempts the auditor of the company from, or indemnifies the auditor against, a liability`
       AND `the liability is one which by law would otherwise attach to the auditor`
       AND `the liability is in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust of which the auditor may be guilty in relation to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any provision ... for exempting any auditor of the company from, or indemnifying the auditor against, any liability which by law would otherwise attach to the auditor in respect of any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust ... is void" is a scope limit with no "only" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

-- (2): "This section does not prevent a company from indemnifying such auditor against any liability incurred or that will be incurred by the auditor -- (a) in defending any proceedings (whether civil or criminal) in which judgment is
-- given in the auditor's favour or in which the auditor is acquitted; or (b) in connection with any application under section 76A(13) or 391 or any other provision of this Act, in which relief is granted to the auditor by the court."
-- src:20082 | (2) This section does not prevent a company from indemnifying
-- src:20083 | such auditor against any liability incurred or that will be incurred by
-- src:20084 | the auditor —
-- src:20089 | (a) in defending any proceedings (whether civil or criminal) in
-- src:20090 | which judgment is given in the auditor’s favour or in which
-- src:20091 | the auditor is acquitted; or
-- src:20093 | (b) in connection with any application under section 76A(13)
-- src:20094 | or 391 or any other provision of this Act, in which relief is
-- src:20095 | granted to the auditor by the court.
@ref s 208A(2) (src:20082-20095)
GIVEN `the indemnity is against a liability incurred or that will be incurred by the auditor in defending proceedings (whether civil or criminal)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment is given in the auditor's favour in those proceedings or the auditor is acquitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indemnity is against a liability incurred or that will be incurred by the auditor in connection with an application under section 76A(13) or 391 or any other provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `relief is granted to the auditor by the court in that application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 208A(2) the section does not prevent the company from indemnifying the auditor` MEANS
    IF     (`the indemnity is against a liability incurred or that will be incurred by the auditor in defending proceedings (whether civil or criminal)` AND `judgment is given in the auditor's favour in those proceedings or the auditor is acquitted`)
        OR (`the indemnity is against a liability incurred or that will be incurred by the auditor in connection with an application under section 76A(13) or 391 or any other provision of this Act` AND `relief is granted to the auditor by the court in that application`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not prevent a company from indemnifying such auditor against any liability incurred ... (a) in defending any proceedings ... in which judgment is given in the auditor's favour or in which the auditor is acquitted; or (b) in connection with any application ... in which relief is granted to the auditor by the court" gives the carve-out on those conditions and says nothing of another indemnity (subsection (1) answers)

-- Together: a provision that subsection (2) lets through is not made void by the section.
@ref s 208A(2) (src:20082-20095)
GIVEN `the section does not prevent the company from indemnifying the auditor under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 208A(1) and (2) the provision is void under the section` MEANS
    IF `the section does not prevent the company from indemnifying the auditor under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not prevent a company from indemnifying such auditor against any liability incurred or that will be incurred by the auditor" (subsection (2): a flat negative, so the section does not make such an indemnity void)
    ELSE `the answer under subsection (1)`
